#====================================================================
# E321 - Make optional acceleration backends explicit in static packages
#====================================================================

id:                     E412
trigger_tool:           configure|conan|ld
phase:                  configuration|linking|packaging
error_signature:        OpenSSL library not found|cannot find -lcrypto|undefined reference to (EVP_|MD5_|SHA)|optional OpenSSL backend auto-detected

severity:               2
category:               configure, linking, dependencies, reproducibility
match_keywords:         optional dependency, OpenSSL, libcrypto, configure autodetect, static package, undeclared dependency, worker environment
title:                  Make optional acceleration backends explicit in self-contained static packages

root_cause:             Configure scripts can auto-detect an optional acceleration library from the build worker even when it is absent from the Conan dependency graph. The resulting static package then varies by worker or exposes undeclared link requirements. Disabling the backend is valid only when upstream provides complete internal implementations and the backend changes performance rather than functionality.
affected_scope:         C and C++ projects with internal implementations plus configure-time optional crypto, compression, or SIMD backends, especially self-contained static Conan packages.
verification_cmd:       conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<target-profile> -pr:b=<target-profile> --build='*' && run upstream tests and inspect the packaged archive and consumer link line for undeclared libraries

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           explicit-optional-backend-policy
rec_description:        Decide the optional backend policy in the recipe instead of accepting host autodetection. For a dependency-free static package whose upstream internal implementation retains every public feature, disable an acceleration-only backend and document the boundary. If the backend supplies required functionality, declare it as a Conan requirement and enable it explicitly.
rec_command:            ./configure --disable-openssl --enable-static --disable-lib-shared && make -j1 test test-lib
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-option-and-dependency-policy

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      explicit-conan-option-with-backend-requirement
fallback_description:   Expose a package option for the backend, add the matching Conan requirement when enabled, and pass its include and link metadata explicitly so the result never depends on worker-installed libraries.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       configure.*auto.*openssl|OPENSSL_FOUND=found.*requirements.*\[\]
forbid_1_reason:        Host autodetection bypasses the Conan dependency graph and makes static link requirements environment-dependent.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package can pass on one worker and fail for consumers or on another worker with missing libcrypto symbols.
forbid_2_pattern:       disable-openssl.*required functionality|disable.*backend.*tests skipped
forbid_2_reason:        A required security or protocol feature must not be removed merely to make the build pass.
forbid_2_consequence:   The package builds but violates its advertised public functionality.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

